(Current HTML pattern validation is defined using the JavaScript regular-expression v \(Unicode sets\) mode, which has) Tj
T* (stricter character-class syntax than the historical default mode. A pattern that works with new RegExp\(pattern\) can still be) Tj
T* (rejected by an HTML input. Testing with the browser's actual pattern/checkValidity behavior is more representative than) Tj
T* (testing only with a default-flag RegExp.) Tj
